  "details": "Show Avatars Performance Rank on Name Tags with a Big icon for the Max Performance Rank and a Small Performance Icon for the Average.\n\nie ( Big Medium, Small Excellent. )\n\nHowever 2 values are shown when selecting a user. The Avatars Highest Average Performance Rank and the Maximum Performance Rank (Maximum Perf Rank being how it currently works) with a percentage on both icons\n\n ie ( `Excellent Icon` 68% `Medium Icon` 10% )\n\n\nWhen viewing Avatar Stats, it will show all percentages.\n\nie (`Excellent` 68%, `Good` 22%, `Medium` 10%, `Poor` 0%, `Very Poor` 0% )\n\nMight need some small communication to the User but it may help people have a better drive to optimise the rest of their avatars if they can't get around some restrictions like Audio or some dynamic bone usage, Without needed to change how the Safety side of things operate. (As it will use the Maximum Performance Ranking to base security off of) It could also be a good at a glance for an avatars \"Actual stats\" as the above examples is how I see alot of users stats, with a majority of the avatar actually being Excellent. (So mainly just a UI feature and not a system change)\n(A bonus could be that the percentage could be influence by the values themselves and how close or far they are from each rankings passing numbers. like 1 skinned mesh > 4 skinned meshes)",
